Date:   Sat Oct 10 13:29:18 2026 +0300

    fix(1380): discharge the rework verdict — honest footers, branch-true caps, E5 screen, bounded spans

    All 4 blocking + 4 important items from the 5-leg rework review, plus
    the API-hygiene suggestions:

    - obligations_ledger_test: drop the duplicate 'payload' local (the
      suite failed to load).
    - session_search_test: '_giantText' is final — 'x' * 2000 is not a
      const expression (the suite failed to load).
    - agent_cli_prompt_recall_test: import prompts.g.dart for
      recallHygienePrompt (the suite failed to load); boot the prompt
      through the model-seen context seam — the old cli.systemPrompt read
      raced the composer after the wiring refactor; drive the tool-surface
      turn instead of polling a busy flag that settles between polls.
    - formatSessionSearchOutcome: the truncation/continuation footer
      survives the zero-hit page (a capped or time-budgeted scan with no
      hits on this page never again reads as 'no records match'), and a
      new SessionSearchOutcome.unavailableReason prints verbatim when no
      archive could be searched at all — the CLI's no-session-file
      degradation says so instead of claiming an empty scan.
    - the result cap counts TRUE branch hits only: branch scope resolves
      the archive's final active branch on a cheap structure-only census
      pass (the same pattern map mode already pays) and seeds the real
      pass, so abandoned-fork matches never consume the cap and the default
      scope delivers full 40-hit pages. This also fixes a latent bug the
      census exposed: the active leaf pinned to the FIRST record, so branch
      scope silently matched the root record alone.
    - the active leaf now tracks the storage's own semantics (every append
      becomes the tip unless a LeafRecord moves it).
    - E5: nested-quantifier regexes are rejected at parse time (the
      classic catastrophic-backtracking shape; escapes, classes and
      non-capturing group syntax respected), and the cap/budget docs state
      the honest boundary — the wall clock is checked BETWEEN records, the
      128 KB cap bounds one match, ambiguous-alternation shapes stay
      unscreened by design.
    - the checkpoint ordinal table is seeded from a census of the ids
      checkpoints actually reference (bounded), the map fold builds its
      list once, time-budget stops now carry a continuation token (any
      clean stop pages), and the retention claim is corrected in the docs:
      the parent map is one id pair per record — ids, never content.
    - scanSessionSegment is library-private (the private-type-in-public-API
      finding; it was barrel-exported).
    - recordPendingWait's degradation outcomes are logged, not discarded,
      and the schedule_message result line carries the cross-tool contract
      comment.
    - maxHits clamp test input actually exceeds the ceiling now.

